    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the change so that creating an owner returns a `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `displayName` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema. Since the DTOs (`OwnerDto`) are generated from this OpenAPI spec at build time, this makes `displayName` part of the serialized owner response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct mapping on `toOwnerDto(Owner)` that computes the field from the stored names:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   ```\n\nBecause `getOwner` and `addOwner` both go through `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(...)`, the `displayName` is now populated on every owner response. The acceptance test (`coreComputesDisplayName`) and the full suite pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
